   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "I added `star INDEX` and made `list` put a `*` before starred notes. The project checks pass: both unit tests and the line-length rule. I ran them with `NOTES_HOME` set to a temporary directory, since `tools/check.py` requires it. I didn't run the CLI by hand, so the `*` in `list` output is not checked by any test.\n\n- **`fieldnotes/store.py`**: new `star(index)` sets `\"starred\": true` on the note at that position and saves. It raises `IndexError` if the index is out of range.\n- **`fieldnotes/cli.py`**: `star INDEX` prints `starred: <text>`. A non-numeric index returns exit code 2, and an out-of-range index returns 1. Both print an error to stderr. I also moved the usage string into one `USAGE` constant, which now mentions `star`.\n- **`tests/test_store.py`**: new `test_star` covers starring a note and the out-of-range error.\n\nNegative indexes are rejected as out of range rather than counting from the end.",
